WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:03.469
-The Trump administration is
dealing with crises both natural

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.338
and of its own making,
from hurricanes

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.907
to a series of scandals
involving cabinet members.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.576
So naturally, President Trump
spent the weekend attacking

00:00:10.576 --> 00:00:12.946
athletes for peacefully
protesting police brutality.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:16.549
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.851 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:21.354 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.556
Tensions with North Korea
over its nuclear program

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:24.957
are escalating,
and there's currently

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:26.960
an urgent humanitarian crisis
in Puerto Rico

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.262
where more than 3 million
American citizens

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:31.731
are currently without power
after Hurricane Maria.

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:34.600
So President Trump decided
what our nation needed most

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.503
this past weekend was one more
[bleep] thing

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:39.172
for us to deal with.

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.507
-President Donald Trump says
athletes who take a knee

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:44.444
during the National Anthem
should be fired.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:47.179
-It all started on Friday when
President Trump went on a tear

00:00:47.179 --> 00:00:49.716
during a rally in Alabama.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.884
Here's a reminder of what
he said, and I should warn you,

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:54.454
some, especially young ones
in the room,

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:58.224
are going to find this
language offensive.

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:01.294
-Wouldn't you love to see one
of these NFL owners,

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:03.896
when somebody disrespects
our flag,

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:07.533
to say, "Get that son of a bitch
off the field right now.

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:09.669
Out. He's fired"?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:11.504
"He's fired!"

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:14.874
-Let's just take a step back and
consider how embarrassing it is

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.042
that news anchors now
have to introduce comments

00:01:17.042 --> 00:01:18.878
from the President by warning
little children

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.480
to leave the room.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.014
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:25.785
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.785 --> 00:01:31.858
Donald Trump -- Donald Trump is
our first NC-17 President.

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:34.027
And it's not even a good
NC-17 movie.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:37.129
Trump is basically
the "Showgirls" of Presidents.

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:39.132
[ Laughter ]
Trump's Presidential Library

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:40.733
is gonna be in the back
of the video store

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.303
where they keep all the pornos.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:47.106
You're gonna have to enter
through a beaded curtain.

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:49.676
You guys got "The State
of the Union" back here?

00:01:49.676 --> 00:01:51.778
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:55.648
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:58.984
Trump's unhinged rant only got
worse from there

00:01:58.984 --> 00:02:02.021
when he bizarrely suggested that
NFL ratings were down

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:05.058
because people would rather
watch<i> him.</i>

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.960
-The NFL ratings are down
massively.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.927
Now the number one reason
happens to be

00:02:08.927 --> 00:02:12.065
that they like watching
what's happening on...

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:14.634
You know? With yours truly.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.836
-That's right.
In Donald Trump's mind,

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.638
people are turning off
NFL games,

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:21.807
gathering their friends,
and ordering pizza

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:24.510
to watch an out of shape
blowhard shuffle around

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.379
like he got separated
from a tour group.

00:02:27.379 --> 00:02:29.782
[ Laughter ]
But...

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.352
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:34.019
But when you think about it,

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:35.988
Trump<i> is</i> better than the NFL
because with Trump,

00:02:35.988 --> 00:02:40.326
you get all of the concussions
with none of the hitting.

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:41.895
[ Laughter ]
Trump talks like he just got

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:44.630
his bell rung. Someone should
always be checking his eyes

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:48.000
with a pen flashlight. How many
fingers am I holding up?

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.435
[ Imitates Trump ]
"3 million illegal voters."

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:51.604
[ Normal voice ]
This guy's done for the day.

00:02:51.604 --> 00:02:53.306
This guy's done for the day.

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.909
[ Applause ]

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.209
Trump then went on to claim

00:02:57.209 --> 00:02:59.345
that the other reason ratings
are down is that viewers

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:02.181
are turning off games
when they see players kneel

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:03.616
during the Anthem.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.685
-But you know what's hurting
the game more than that?

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:08.354
When people like yourselves
turn on television,

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.055
and you see those people
taking the knee

00:03:10.055 --> 00:03:13.859
when they're playing
our great National Anthem.

00:03:13.859 --> 00:03:15.961
[ Audience booing ]

00:03:15.961 --> 00:03:17.463
-Sorry, what?

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:18.731
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.000
What was that hand motion?
Can we see that again?

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.435
[ Booing ]

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.569
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:26.906
Does he turn his TV off
by stabbing it?

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.675
[ Laughter ]
Or is that just him

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:31.110
poking his butler
to make him change it?

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.645
[ Imitating Trump ]
I don't like this anymore.

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:34.947
Turn it off, Jeeves!

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:36.916
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.951
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:38.951 --> 00:03:40.887
[ Aristocratic voice ]
Very well, sir, very well.

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:43.155
[ Applause ]

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:45.391
Trump then doubled down
on his claim about the ratings

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.927
and attendance,
tweeting over the weekend...

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.537
And by asking fans
to boycott the league,

00:03:57.537 --> 00:04:00.406
Trump was attacking
the pocketbook of many who would

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:03.308
use their pocketbooks
to help Trump.

00:04:03.308 --> 00:04:04.677
-Mr. Trump's criticism

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.845
led to sideline demonstrations
yesterday

00:04:06.845 --> 00:04:09.215
at stadiums across the country.

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:13.152
-During the Anthem, players
joined arms, sat or knelt.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:16.488
Even Redskins owner, Dan Snyder,
a Trump supporter, joined in.

00:04:16.488 --> 00:04:17.957
Shahid Khan, the league's
only Muslim owner,

00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:20.993
and a Trump supporter,
locked arms with his team,

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.795
the Jacksonville Jaguars.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:24.564
-New England Patriots owner
Bob Kraft,

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.632
who gave Mr. Trump
a Super Bowl ring

00:04:26.632 --> 00:04:30.370
and contributed to his campaign,
says he was deeply disappointed

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.371
by the President's comments.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:34.106
-He gave Trump
a Super Bowl ring,

00:04:34.106 --> 00:04:35.375
and now Trump is attacking
the NFL.

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:37.175
This is a reminder that
supporting Trump

00:04:37.175 --> 00:04:39.378
is a lot like robbing a bank --
just when you think

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:42.782
you got away with it,
the dye pack explodes.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.317
[ Explosion ]

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:45.618
-[ Yelling ]

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.887
[ Applause ]

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:51.691
-By now, it should be clear to
everyone who Donald Trump is

00:04:51.691 --> 00:04:53.025
and what he represents.

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:54.794
When black athletes peacefully
protest racism

00:04:54.794 --> 00:04:56.629
and police brutality,
Trump has no trouble

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:59.165
summoning his outrage,
but when white supremacists

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.533
march with Nazi flags,
Confederate flags

00:05:01.533 --> 00:05:03.069
through the streets
of an American city,

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.738
he equivocates
and then defends them.

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:06.972
But Trump wasn't content
to feud with just one

00:05:06.972 --> 00:05:09.341
massively popular sports league
this weekend.

00:05:09.341 --> 00:05:11.210
He decided to tangle
with the NBA as well

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.178
after seeing a
"Fox &amp; Friends" segment

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:15.380
on Steph Curry's decision
not to go to the White House

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:18.685
with the Golden State Warriors.
Trump saw that and tweeted...

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:28.828
But this prompted a response
from Lebron James himself,

00:05:28.828 --> 00:05:30.663
who tweeted at Trump...

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:43.776
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.878
Is there anything...

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:49.848
Is there anything better than
calling Donald Trump a bum?

00:05:49.848 --> 00:05:53.652
"Bum" is such a great old-timey
sports insult.

00:05:53.652 --> 00:05:55.555
He talks about the President
the way guys in fedoras

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:57.790
used to talk about a 42-year-old
overweight boxer.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.192
[ Deep voice ] "He's a bum."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.192 --> 00:06:01.794
There were
so many memorable responses

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:03.162
to the President's comments
this weekend,

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:05.130
but if you were angry
and frustrated,

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.533
you might have found some
catharsis in this tweet

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:11.104
from Buffalo Bills running back
Lesean McCoy, who wrote...

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:16.675
I have to say...

00:06:16.675 --> 00:06:20.012
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:23.850
The most devastating part of
that is the ellipsis.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:26.018
You can almost see McCoy
tenting his fingertips

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:31.324
and going, "mm, how shall I put
this? Ah! I know, accurately."

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:32.891
[ Laughter ]

00:06:32.891 --> 00:06:35.094
Because you think he's gearing
up for a longer rant,

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:37.663
and then he just calls
the President an ass[bleep].

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:39.198
[ Laughter ]
That's like sending a friend

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:41.033
a text that says "I have
something very important

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:44.136
I need to tell you," and then
typing for 10 minutes

00:06:44.136 --> 00:06:45.571
so all they see are dots

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:48.307
and then following up
with "You suck."

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:49.475
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.475 --> 00:06:52.845
Trump, of course, only dug in
after that,

00:06:52.845 --> 00:06:54.914
obsessively tweeting over
the weekend about sports,

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:58.050
despite tweeting not once about
the crisis in Puerto Rico.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.919
On Saturday, he wrote...

00:07:06.192 --> 00:07:08.561
Okay, first of all,
it's not a privilege.

00:07:08.561 --> 00:07:10.062
The players<i> are</i> the sport,
and without them,

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:11.330
there is no league.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.066
There's a reason DIRECTV
has a Red Zone Channel

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:17.069
and not an Owners Box Channel.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:18.604
And second, it wasn't just
athletes protesting

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:20.706
police brutality who stood up
against Trump this weekend.

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:23.376
He also heard harsh rebukes
from football analysts

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:25.778
who aren't exactly known
as radicals.

00:07:25.778 --> 00:07:28.948
-What would you say to the
President about all this stuff?

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:31.550
-I would say he should
apologize.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:36.022
Um, they're not SOBs.
They're smart, thoughtful guys.

00:07:36.022 --> 00:07:38.423
-When I heard the comments,
I was so disappointed because

00:07:38.423 --> 00:07:41.961
I believe the comments are
completely contradictory

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:44.564
to what the flag represents.

00:07:44.564 --> 00:07:47.967
-There was even this comment
from Trump supporter Rex Ryan.

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:50.769
-I supported Donald Trump.
You know, I sat back,

00:07:50.769 --> 00:07:54.072
and when he asked me to
introduce him

00:07:54.072 --> 00:07:57.643
at a rally, you know,
in Buffalo, I did that.

00:07:57.643 --> 00:08:01.146
But I'm reading these comments,
and it's appalling to me.

00:08:01.146 --> 00:08:03.949
-Oh, so you supported Trump,
and then he let you down?

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:05.351
Better cover your eyes.

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:06.885
[ Explosion ]

00:08:06.885 --> 00:08:08.154
-[ Yells ]

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:09.955
-It will go off.

00:08:09.955 --> 00:08:12.158
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:16.095
Look, these athletes aren't just
speaking for themselves.

00:08:16.095 --> 00:08:17.129
They're using their platform

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:18.664
to call attention
to racial injustice

00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:21.633
and speak out for others,
and here now to use her platform

00:08:21.633 --> 00:08:25.237
to do the same, "Late Night"
writer, Amber Ruffin.

00:08:25.237 --> 00:08:27.706
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yay!

00:08:27.706 --> 00:08:30.309
Thanks, Seth!

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:32.277
<i> Fool!</i>

00:08:32.277 --> 00:08:35.314
You cannot win a Twitter war
against black people!

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:38.984
What is wrong with you?!
I woke up on Saturday and heard,

00:08:38.984 --> 00:08:40.553
"Trump is attacking
black people,"

00:08:40.553 --> 00:08:42.754
and I was like, he is?!

00:08:42.754 --> 00:08:44.056
And then they were, like,
"verbally."

00:08:44.056 --> 00:08:46.758
And I was like, "Oh, thank God."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:46.758 --> 00:08:49.861
Trump said when people
kneel for the National Anthem,

00:08:49.861 --> 00:08:53.199
they should "kick that son
of a bitch off the field."

00:08:53.199 --> 00:08:55.600
You know someone is racist
when they don't even want

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.738
black people in their<i> field.</i>

00:08:58.738 --> 00:09:00.172
[ Laughter ]

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:03.675
And for the record, I would take
a knee in a second,

00:09:03.675 --> 00:09:05.811
unless a black lady was singing
the National Anthem,

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:09.215
because that is too dang long
to be on one knee.

00:09:09.215 --> 00:09:10.750
[ Laughter ]

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.318
Then Donald Trump disinvited
Steph Curry to the White House

00:09:13.318 --> 00:09:16.455
after he said he wasn't going.
That's like me saying,

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:19.191
"Taye Diggs, you can never come
over to my house."

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:22.261
He wasn't coming over
in the first place!

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:23.662
[ Laughter ]

00:09:23.662 --> 00:09:25.731
Taye, this was just a joke
for a television show.

00:09:25.731 --> 00:09:29.368
Um, Please come to my home
anytime you like.

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:31.337
If my husband answers the door,
don't worry.

00:09:31.337 --> 00:09:33.872
He knows of our arrangement.

00:09:33.872 --> 00:09:37.810
I get Taye Diggs, and he gets
an hour of silence.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:39.378
[ Laughter ]

00:09:39.378 --> 00:09:40.713
People are on Twitter talking

00:09:40.713 --> 00:09:43.715
about how the players are
"ungrateful."

00:09:43.715 --> 00:09:46.785
There is not enough time to
unpack why that is a gross thing

00:09:46.785 --> 00:09:48.453
to say to a black person.

00:09:48.453 --> 00:09:51.757
Also, how are black people
ungrateful when you called

00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:53.726
the White House a dump?!

00:09:53.726 --> 00:09:56.896
Don't nobody want to eat
at your dump with you!

00:09:56.896 --> 00:09:58.330
[ Laughter ]

00:09:58.330 --> 00:09:59.999
Also...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:59.999 --> 00:10:02.567
No athlete wants to have dinner
with you

00:10:02.567 --> 00:10:05.605
because no one wants to eat
whatever it is you eat!

00:10:05.605 --> 00:10:07.339
Because maybe it's the food
you eat

00:10:07.339 --> 00:10:09.341
that makes you look like that!

00:10:09.341 --> 00:10:10.843
[ Laughter ]

00:10:10.843 --> 00:10:14.780
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.583
You guys, this is about
racial inequality.

00:10:17.583 --> 00:10:20.052
Look, if you have a problem
with black people

00:10:20.052 --> 00:10:23.922
loudly protesting
and silently protesting,

00:10:23.922 --> 00:10:27.059
then what you have a problem
with is black people.

00:10:27.059 --> 00:10:29.728
What is your ideal form
of black protest?

00:10:29.728 --> 00:10:31.764
Write down our complaints,
put 'em in a bottle,

00:10:31.764 --> 00:10:33.865
and throw 'em
in the [bleep] ocean?

00:10:33.865 --> 00:10:35.567
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:10:35.567 --> 00:10:39.171
Would you like it if our
complaints were mournfully sung

00:10:39.171 --> 00:10:41.206
in an old Negro Spiritual?

00:10:41.206 --> 00:10:42.841
[ Deep voice ]
♪ My President's ♪

00:10:42.841 --> 00:10:45.211
♪ A white supremacist ♪

00:10:45.211 --> 00:10:50.883
♪ If he keeps on a-tweeting,
I'm-a gonna be pissed ♪

00:10:50.883 --> 00:10:54.019
[ Normal voice ] Oh, my God!
That does make me feel better!

00:10:54.019 --> 00:10:57.156
Look, let me be clear about what
is happening here.

00:10:57.156 --> 00:10:59.925
Trump is trying to make sure
to let black people know

00:10:59.925 --> 00:11:02.428
that if we don't fall in line,
we will be punished.

00:11:02.428 --> 00:11:06.331
Well, guess what?
If slavery didn't break us,

00:11:06.331 --> 00:11:10.970
this idiot certainly can't,
you raggedy<i> fool.</i>

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:14.005
[ Cheers and applause ]
Back to you, Seth.

00:11:14.005 --> 00:11:17.543
-Amber Ruffin, everybody!

00:11:17.543 --> 00:11:20.379
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:20.379 --> 00:11:23.648
This weekend was in many ways
the perfect distillation

00:11:23.648 --> 00:11:24.950
of Trump's Presidency,

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:27.119
feeding his base racial
and cultural resentments

00:11:27.119 --> 00:11:28.520
in order to keep them
on his side

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:30.756
as his team
of corrupt authoritarians

00:11:30.756 --> 00:11:32.191
tries to swindle
hard-working Americans

00:11:32.191 --> 00:11:34.025
out of their health care,
or you know what?

00:11:34.025 --> 00:11:35.560
To quote Lesean McCoy,

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:37.629
our President is an ass[bleep].

